{"name":"Midori","hex":"#2a603b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Midori","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweet, bright green, muskmelon-flavored liqueur made by Suntory."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Japanese.","A unisex given name from Japanese."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Midori"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midori, Gunma","blocks":[{"text":"Midori  is a city located in Gunma Prefecture, Japan. As of 31 August 2020, the city had an estimated population of 50,266 in 21,028 households, and a population density of 240 persons per km2. The total area of the city is 208.42 square kilometres (80.47 sq mi)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Midori_city_hall_Kasakake_public_office.JPG/330px-Midori_city_hall_Kasakake_public_office.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midori%2C_Gunma","wikidata":"Q576556"},{"title":"Midori-ku, Chiba","blocks":[{"text":"Midori Ward  is one of the six wards of the city of Chiba in Chiba Prefecture, Japan. As of February 2016, the ward had an estimated population of 127,368 and a population density of 1920 persons per km2. The total area was 66.25 square kilometres (25.58 sq mi)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Midori-Ward_office%2C_Midori-ku%2C_Chiba%2C_Japan.jpg/330px-Midori-Ward_office%2C_Midori-ku%2C_Chiba%2C_Japan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midori-ku%2C_Chiba","wikidata":"Q926492"},{"title":"Midori (liqueur)","blocks":[{"text":"Midori  is a sweet, bright green-colored liqueur made by Suntory, flavored with Yubari King and muskmelon."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midori_(liqueur)","wikidata":"Q1271521"},{"title":"Midori (violinist)","blocks":[{"text":"Midori Goto , who performs under the mononym Midori, is a Japanese-born American violinist. She made her debut with the New York Philharmonic at age 11 as a surprise guest soloist at the New Year's Eve Gala in 1982. In 1986 her performance at the Tanglewood Music Festival with Leonard Bernstein conducting his own composition made the front-page headlines in The New York Times. Midori became a celebrated child prodigy, and one of the world's preeminent violinists as an adult."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/Midori_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midori_(violinist)","wikidata":"Q268644"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/MountAkagi.jpg/500px-MountAkagi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/MountAkagi.jpg/1280px-MountAkagi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/MountAkagi.jpg/500px-MountAkagi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Akagi and then outskirts of Kiryū and Midori cities","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMountAkagi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Iwajuku-A.jpg/500px-Iwajuku-A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Iwajuku-A.jpg/1280px-Iwajuku-A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Iwajuku-A.jpg/500px-Iwajuku-A.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Iwajuku ruins","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIwajuku-A.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/%E5%9C%B0%E5%9B%B3-%E5%8D%83%E8%91%89%